  "optimizer": "Fresh Adam, unit decoder columns after each step, frozen normalization and native weights.",
  "target_design": "Reuse M18 training-only expandedpair/source schedules and naturaldocuments. Six taskupdates/family, exactly3prefix/3task. One fixed hash-selected group per endpoint, same group index for scalar/block at a seed. Decode delta from starting M18-expanded checkpoint on native MLP1write. Hold delta detached/fixed throughout training. No group rejection if inactive, zero directions retained. All gate eligibility from M17 train/train only.",
  "response_loss": "For final-position logits, let rN=logsoftmax(native perturbed)-logsoftmax(native intact); rF similarly for reconstructed perturbed/intact using identical frozen delta. R=sum_v pN_intact(v)*(rF(v)-rN(v))^2. Differentiate BOTH reconstructed forwards; native outputs and delta detached. Intact loss K=mean all-position/full-vocabulary KL(native||reconstruction).",
  "calibration": "Before optimization, compute Kbar and Rbar at starting checkpoint over all120 scheduled task endpoints, equally weighted including repeats/noops. Freeze lambda=Kbar/Rbar so initial task-average KL and weighted response contributions match. If either nonpositive or nonfinite, fail prerequisite rather than replace/clip. Natural updates use only KL. Task objective control K vs treatment K+lambda*R, equal endpoint weights. This is training-only scaling, not eval-based tuning; gradients and total objective scale need not match.",
  "evaluation": "Initial and final output fidelity on unchanged M18 inventory. Causal validation retains M18/M11-based 704 frozen native directions, source/context/site/group selection and teacher effects unchanged, so training perturbations do not define evaluation deltas. Compare both regions, allthree nontrainingquadrants, family weighting, raw errors and native energy denominators. Whole-task exclusions preserved.",
  "gradient_checks": "For each startingmodel and eachregion, first scheduled endpoint with nonzero delta and positive response loss. Check q=native identity response, finite differences at eps1e-3 and3e-4 along normalized analytic gradient scaled by qnorm; relative tolerance3% or absolute1e-6. Check both reconstructed branches require gradients and frozen native parameters/delta do not. Then test finite nonzero featurizer gradients through selectedsupport. Gate index derivatives are not claimed.",
  "stopping_rule": "Generate targets/calibrate/audit before training. Exactly8fits at120updates; no responseweight/group/template/width search. Train-only scaling may create numericaldifficulty; failures retained and any repair documented separately. Causal-transfer gain is necessary evidence, not semanticunit/newtaskdiscovery proof.",
  "M25_sha256": "17a3e1780c49eac9bc1c96b7b4ed82446fef8a6ce59627cb8b7bd4d63e93ee2f",
  "evaluation_scope": "All16 live M25 candidates plus4 initials, no selection. Fixed M18/M11 native directions, full existing evaluation inventory. Familiar development data; preserve whole task exclusions."
